1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 { This is the starting point of this chapter. With the 2.Nc3 White can opt for three different setups: 1) Some kind of delayed Bishop's Opening with Bc4 2) The Glek Opening with g3 3) Vienna Gambit with f4. } Nc6 { 2...Nf6 is much more popular but we want to have ...f5 move against the Glek Opening. } 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. d3 { The only independent try. Much more popular 4.Nf3 just transposes to Four Knights with 4.Bc4. } Na5 { Just going for the important bishop. } 5. Bb3 Nxb3 6. axb3 d5 { Let's fight for the centre and open the game for our mighty bishops. } 7. exd5 { -KEY- } Nxd5 8. Nf3 Nxc3 9. bxc3 Bd6 { Black has nice bishops and good central control. } 10. O-O O-O 11. Re1 Re8 $11 { Black can follow up with ...Bg4 or ...b6, ...Bb7. In such structure a useful move could be also ...a5. } 
